      "sprk_agreementtypeid": "d557c894-908c-f111-8077-7ced8ddc4cc6",
      "sprk_classificationcue": "Agreement whose PRIMARY subject is confidentiality / non-disclosure obligations protecting confidential information exchanged during discussions, due diligence, or a business relationship. Distinguishing signals: a defined 'Confidential Information' term, disclosure/use restrictions, standard exclusions (already known, public, independently developed, rightfully received from a third party), a stated term/survival period, and NO substantive license, sale, service, or employment obligations beyond the mutual promise to protect information. Classify as nda ONLY when confidentiality protection is the document's principal purpose -- not when it is a single clause embedded in a broader deal (e.g. an employment or services agreement that happens to include a confidentiality clause); those route to their own sub-domain instead.",
